e than 50 minutes. American " [:a {:href "/athletes/63989"} "Harry Van Bergen"] " sailed his 102-ton “Formosa” into third place. Also entered was the German " [:a {:href "/athletes/12064"} "Max Guilleaume"] ", who had previously competed in equestrianism, in the " [:a {:href "/results/185004"} "four-in-hand event"] ". His yacht “Clara” would have been the largest, at 181 tons."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Official Report of the Games and contemporary newspaper reports record only the owner, Quentin, but there were around 20 unknown crew aboard, and Quentin regularly used master mariners to captain his yachts. Jesse Cranfield, from the town of Rowhedge, Essex, was Quentin’s regular captain in major competitions for many years before and after the Paris Olympics, although it has not yet been possible to prove he sailed the boat at the Games."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Adjusted Time"] [:th {} "Actual Time"] [:th {} "Handicap"] [:th {} "Weight"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Cicely"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "5-29:46"] [:td {} "6-01:06"] [:td {} "-31:20"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "12"} [:a {:href "/athletes/63383"} "Cecil Quentin"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Brynhild"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "5-30:06"] [:td {} "5-30:06"] [:td {} "0:00"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "12"} [:a {:href "/ath